### B. Typography

Typography is applied automatically to standard semantic tags (`h1`, `h2`, `h3`, `h4`, `h5`, `h6`, `p`, `a`, `input`, `textarea`, `select`) by `global.css` (including fully responsive sizing for mobile and desktop screens).

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Typography Inheritance Enforcement**:
> DO NOT write redundant inline typography overrides (e.g. `text-[44px] md:text-[68px] font-bold font-urbanist`) on standard tags. Let them inherit styles directly from the global stylesheet. Override classes (e.g. `text-brand-dark` or `mt-6`) should only be used for structural, color, or margin offsets. Do not duplicate sizes, line-heights, fonts, or weights.

- **Primary Font**: `Urbanist` (sans-serif fallback) — Used for headings, body copy, and primary navigation elements.
  - Tailwind: `font-sans` / `font-heading` / `font-urbanist`
- **Secondary Font**: `Inter` (sans-serif fallback) — Used exclusively for form inputs, textareas, and highly technical or tabular content.
  - Tailwind: `font-inter`

