## 4. Coding & Implementation Rules

### 1. Visual Integrity & Token Enforcement

- **No Hardcoded Hex Values**: Never type arbitrary inline hex values (e.g. `bg-[#abc]`). You must use the utility classes mapped above (e.g., `bg-electric-lime`, `bg-brand-dark`, `border-light-neutral`).
- **Mode Compatibility**: When designing layouts, ensure they are fully responsive to dark mode by testing them with both `bg-background` and `text-foreground`.
- **Accent Contrast Rules**: Do not place Electric Lime (`#CDF660`) text on white or pale backgrounds; it fails contrast checks. Use Electric Lime only as a background with deep-black text (`text-deep-black`) or as high-contrast elements on Brand Dark (`#0E1201`) surfaces.

### 2. Layout & Spacing Discipline

- **Whitespace is deliberate**: Do not pack components together. Ensure standard card container padding is `p-8` (`32px`) and sections are separated by at least `py-12` (`48px`) or `py-[60px]`.
- **Card Border Norms**: Default card surfaces must have a thin, distinct boundary (`border border-light-neutral dark:border-brand-dark/20`) and standard corner rounding (`rounded-lg`).

### 3. Responsive Scaling Rules

All grids and structures must design from mobile-first upwards:

- **Columns**: desktop 3-columns (`grid-cols-3`) must collapse to 2-columns on tablet (`md:grid-cols-2`) and a single column on mobile (`grid-cols-1`).
- **Margins**: Section padding must use `px-6` (`30px` side margins) on mobile viewports, scaling up to `lg:px-[60px]` on standard and large desktops.
- **Header Navigation**: Navigation items collapse to a burger icon below `768px` (tablet). The desktop navigation uses horizontal spacing with `gap-10` (`40px`).

### 4. Interactive Components & Micro-interactions

- All hover states must have active state configurations (e.g., `hover:bg-[#B8E650] active:bg-[#A0D640]` on primary buttons).
- Use `transition-all duration-200` to prevent jarring snap transitions.
- Interactive controls must adhere to accessible touch targets: minimum height/width `44px` on mobile screens.

### 5. SEO & Structural Semantics

- Ensure exactly **one** dynamic `<h1>` per page.
- Heading elements must represent a clean sequential tree (`h1` -> `h2` -> `h3` -> `h4` etc.).
- Add proper `id` properties to all major section wrappers and buttons for clean browser automation and navigation triggers.

